    "name": "Kanso layout - Corne 3x6 keyboard",
    "author": "https://github.com/y4le",
    "notes": "- base layer\n  - qwerty isn't the ideal layout but we want to make use of existing muscle memory wherever possible\n- number/symbol layer\n  - numbers and symbols use same fingers as normal keyboard for muscle memory\n  - `[]` `{}` `()` `/\\` are on mirrored fingers on home row\n- navigation layer\n  - right hand can use vim keys as arrow keys one handed\n  - left hand is modifiers to be used in conjuntion with arrow keys (e.g. hold \"NAV+d+a\" and press \"l\" to add a word to your selection [\"shift+alt+right\"])\n  - right hand can volup/voldown/play/pause/prev/next one handed\n- mouse layer\n  - mouse key bindings for mouseless navigation\n  - using this regularly is an antipattern and a sign that you need to make better navigation shortcuts",
